          %h2#references References
          %h3#in_ordinary_differential_cohomology In ordinary differential cohomology
          %h4#general General
          %p The definition of the Griffith intermediate Jacobian is due to
          %ul
            %li#Griffiths68a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffiths"}> Phillip Griffiths
                ,
                %em Periods of integrals on algebraic manifolds. I
                Construction and properties of the modular varieties“, American Journal of Mathematics 90 (2): 568–626, (1968) &amp;lbrack;doi:10.2307/2373545, ISSN 0002-9327, JSTOR 2373545, MR 0229641&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Griffiths68b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffiths"}> Phillip Griffiths
                ,
                %em Periods of integrals on algebraic manifolds. II
                Local study of the period mapping“, American Journal of Mathematics 90 (3): 805–865 (1968) &amp;lbrack;doi:10.2307/2373485, ISSN 0002-9327, JSTOR 2373485, summary:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GriffithsPeriodsSummary.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                , MR 0233825 &amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Griffiths12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffiths"}> Phillip Griffiths
                , section 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some results on algebraic cycles on algebraic manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/node/181"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/someresultsonalg.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Haus22"}> Haus (2022), Ch 1
                \.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
            but with generalization to non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
            the Grifiths-like follows also with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
            as discussed in
          %ul
            %li#ScheinostSchottenloher96
              Peter Scheinost,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
              = succeed "," do
                %em Metaplectic quantization of the moduli spaces of flat and parabolic bundles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/153753"} web
          %p The mid-dimensional case was discussed in unpublished work by Lazzeri, see
          %ul
            %li#Rubei98
              Elena Rubei,
              %em Lazzeri’s Jacobian of oriented compact riemannian manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9812110"}> arXiv:math/9812110
              )
          %p
            The relation of the intermediate Jacobian to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            (Deligne’s theorem) due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"} Pierre Deligne
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#EsnaultViehweg88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%A9l%C3%A8ne+Esnault"}> Hélène Esnault
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckart+Viehweg"} Eckart Viehweg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deligne-Beilinson cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rapoport"} Michael Rapoport
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norbert+Schappacher"} Norbert Schappacher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Schneider"} Peter Schneider
              (eds.),
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson%27s+Conjectures+on+Special+Values+of+L-Functions"} Beilinson's Conjectures on Special Values of L-Functions
              Perspectives in Mathematic
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EsnaultViehweg-DeligneBeilinsonCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Reviews and surveys include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.encyclopediaofmath.org/index.php/Intermediate_Jacobian"} Intermediate Jacobian
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intermediate_Jacobian"} Intermediate Jacobian
            %li#Walls12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Walls"}> Patrick Walls
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intermediate Jacobians and Abel-Jacobi maps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WallsJacobian.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Brylinski07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
                , around theorem I 1.5.11 of
                %em Loop Spaces, Characteristic Classes and Geometric Quantization
                Springer, 2007
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variétés de Prym et jacobiennes intermédiaire
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~beauvill/pubs/prym.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=ASENS_1977_4_10_3_309_0"} jstor
            %li
              %p
                Valentin Zakharevich,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mixed Intermediate Jacobians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.algant.eu/documents/theses/zakharevich.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Polishchuk03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polishchuk"}> Alexander Polishchuk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian varieties, Theta functions and the Fourier transform
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math1.unice.fr/~beauvill/pubs/poli.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+structures"} Hodge structures
            includes
          %ul
            %li#PetersSteenbrink08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Peters"}> Chris Peters
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jozef+Steenbrink"} Jozef Steenbrink
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mixed+Hodge+Structures"} Mixed Hodge Structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.arithgeo.ethz.ch/alpbach2012/Peters_Steenbrinck"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/~peters/world.f/Torino.pdf"} pdf
          %h4#for_calabiyau_3folds For Calabi-Yau 3-folds
          %p
            Discussion of intermediate Jacobians of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+3-folds"} Calabi-Yau 3-folds
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                C. Herbert Clemens,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+Griffith"} Phillip Griffith
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The intermediate Jacobian of the cubic threefold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970801"} JSTOR
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claire+Voisin"} Claire Voisin
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.polytechnique.fr/~voisin/Articlesweb/griffithsgroup.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+H%C3%B6ring"}> Andreas Höring
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Minimal classes on the intermediate Jacobian of a generic cubic threefold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~hoering/articles/a5-intermediate.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
          %ul
            %li#GeerKatsura03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerard+van+der+Geer"}> Gerard van der Geer
              , T. Katsura,
              %em On the height of Calabi-Yau varieties in positive characteristic
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0302023"}> arXiv:math/0302023
              )
          %p
            Applications in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li#Morrison95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"}> David Morrison
                , section 4 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mirror Symmetry and the Type II String
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9512016"} arXiv:hep-th/9512016
            %li#DDP06
              %p
                Diaconescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"} Ron Donagi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"} Tony Pantev
                %em Intermediate Jacobians and ADE Hitchin Systems
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607159"}> arXiv:hep-th/0607159
                )
            %li#BKNPP09
              %p
                Ling Bao, Axel Kleinschmidt, Bengt E. W. Nilsson, Daniel Persson, Boris Pioline,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Instanton Corrections to the Universal Hypermultiplet and Automorphic Forms on SU(2,1)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.4299"} arXiv:0909.4299
            %li#Baarsma11
              %p
                A. Baarsma,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The hypermultiplet moduli space of compactified type IIA string theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dspace.library.uu.nl/handle/1874/203182"} web
          %p
            The relation of Theta characteristics on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobians"} intermediate Jacobians
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            was first recognized in
          %ul
            %li#Witten96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Five-Brane Effective Action In M-Theory
              %strong 22
              (1997) 103-133 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610234"}> arXiv:hep-th/9610234
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and the argument there was made rigorous in
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2C+and+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology, and M-Theory
              (2005)
          %h3#for_generalized_cohomology For generalized cohomology
          %p
            Intermediate Jacobians of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            classes were discussed in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            in
          %ul
            %li#Witten99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality Relations Among Topological Effects In String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9912086"} arXiv:hep-th/9912086
            %li#MooreWitten99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"}> Gregory Moore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Self-Duality, Ramond-Ramond Fields, and K-Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9912279"} arXiv:hep-th/9912279
            %li#MW00
              %p
                D. Diaconescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                    Gauge Theory, and a Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005090"} arXiv:hep-th/0005090
                %em A Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005091"}> arXiv:hep-th/0005091
                )
            %li#BelovMooreII
              %p
                Dmitriy Belov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                %em Type II Actions from 11-Dimensional Chern-Simons Theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0611020"}> arXiv:hep-th/0611020
                )
          %p A mathematical discussion inspired by this is in
          %ul
            %li#MPS11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%BCller-Stach"}> Stefan Müller-Stach
              , Chris Peters, Vasudevan Srinivas,
              %em Abelian varieties and theta functions associated to compact Riemannian manifolds; constructions inspired by superstring theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.4108"}> arXiv:1105.4108
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/~peters/world.f/Torino.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p
            Discussion of intermediate Jacobians in generalized
            = succeed ",:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge-filtered+differential+cohomology"} Hodge-filtered differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsQuick12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              ,
